{%- doc -%}
  bmp-structured-data — BMP SEO structured data.

  Emits a schema.org WebSite entity with a SearchAction (the Google "sitelinks
  search box") on the HOME page only. schema.org's WebSite + SearchAction is a
  public, documented standard; self-gated so it adds zero bytes on every other
  page (request.page_type is the canonical Shopify object for this check —
  see Shopify.dev "request" reference).

  The Organization "sameAs" is NOT emitted here — it is injected directly into
  the existing core Organization node (sections/header.liquid) via
  snippets/bmp-org-sameas.liquid behind a BMP-HOOK, so there is exactly ONE
  Organization node site-wide (two would be worse for SEO than none).

  Escaping: every dynamic value is piped through the built-in `json` filter,
  which serializes it as a valid, escaped JSON string literal (quotes,
  backslashes, and control characters are escaped) — the same filter the core
  Organization node in sections/header.liquid already uses for shop.name, so
  the two script blocks share one escaping convention. `escape` is HTML-entity
  escaping (wrong context here — this is JSON-string, not HTML-attribute,
  context) and is not used.

  Rendered once per page from snippets/bmp-globals.liquid. No CSS, no JS.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      request.origin, not shop.url. shop.url is always the store's PRIMARY
      domain, never the host the shopper is actually on, so under Shopify
      Markets international domains a shopper on https://example.fr/ would get
      a WebSite node claiming "url": "https://example.com" and a SearchAction
      target pointing cross-domain, while canonical_url and the sibling
      Organization node both say example.fr. Everywhere else this theme derives
      URLs from the request: sections/header.liquid:323
      (request.origin | append: page.url -- the Organization node this same PR
      edits) and snippets/meta-tags.liquid:23,32. routes.* already carries the
      locale prefix. On a single-domain store request.origin equals shop.url
      and this renders identically; the reason to close it now is that this PR
      would otherwise ship two structured-data nodes in one <head> deriving
      their URL two different ways and agreeing only by coincidence.
    endcomment
    assign bmp_seo_home_url = request.origin | append: routes.root_url
    assign bmp_seo_search_url_template = request.origin | append: routes.search_url | append: '?q={search_term_string}'
  -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "url": {{ bmp_seo_home_url | json }},
      "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
      "potentialAction": {
        "@type": "SearchAction",
        "target": {
          "@type": "EntryPoint",
          "urlTemplate": {{ bmp_seo_search_url_template | json }}
        },
        "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
      }
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
